WEBVTT - Markov Decision Process (MDP)

00:00.000 --> 00:30.000
Decision making under uncertainty is formalized as a Markov Decision Process, defined by states S, actions A, transition probabilities P, rewards R, and a discount factor gamma.

00:30.000 --> 01:05.000
The Markov property dictates that the future state depends solely on the current state and action, not the sequence of past states. The optimal value function satisfies the recursive Bellman Optimality Equation.

01:05.000 --> 01:44.000
MindEase’s Layer 2 Q-learning architecture adopts this foundational formulation: modeling learner behavioral signals into discrete states to compute cumulative engagement rewards.
